-- title:
--   Supersingular base-layer stalks over small constants at q=2
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, and all function fields are realised as subfields of Laurent series. For $N \ge 1$, `modularFunctionFieldFull N` is the subfield of $\mathbb Q((q))$ generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the expansions $\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb Q\,d\,(j_q)$ for all divisors $d \mid N$, and `modularFunctionFieldBar N` is the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ by the coefficientwise image of that field. For a field $\kappa$, `modularFunctionFieldC κ N` is the $\kappa$-subfield of $\kappa((q))$ generated by `jqModC κ` and `jqNModC κ N`, with distinguished element `jGeomGen κ N = jqModC κ`. Finally `fieldBar q M'` is `xHFunctionFieldBar (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the function field of $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$, where $H =$ `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$.
--
--   **Arithmetic data.** A prime $q$ with $q = 2$; an integer $M' \neq 0$ with $q \nmid M'$; a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$ (the rigid-level guard). A valuation subring $A \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$; write $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A`.
--
--   **Supersingular place data.** A finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` over $\kappa$ with `hW`: $w \in W$ if and only if $w \in$ `ssPlaces q M' κ`, that is, $w$ is rational (the structure map $\kappa \to w.\mathrm{ResidueField}$ is surjective), $w$ is an affine geometric place in the sense of `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen}\,\kappa\,M') \in$ `ssJSet q κ`. A chosen element $s \in W$.
--
--   **Reduction data.** An inclusion `hle` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` into `fieldBar q M'`; a constant reduction $R_0$ of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`, i.e. a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, a surjective ring map $R_0.\mathrm{residue}$ onto `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` whose kernel is the maximal ideal, with $\mathrm{algebraMap}\,x \in R_0.\mathrm{integers} \leftrightarrow x \in A$ for constants $x$, compatibility of residues with $A \to \kappa$ on constants, the normalisation that every non-zero $f$ has a constant multiple lying in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ with non-zero residue, together with a map $R_0.\mathrm{placeMap}$ on places preserving degrees and transporting divisors of functions with non-zero residue. The hypothesis `hR₀` requires, for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((q))$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that this image lie in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and that its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, be the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   **Small-constants package.** An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ with $\pi_0 \in A$, such that the contracted ring $A \cap k_0 =$ `A.comap (algebraMap k₀ ℚ̄)` is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), is henselian (`hhens`), and has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`); and `hκ`: every $a \in A$ differs from some $c \in k_0 \cap A$ by an element of the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   **Auxiliary-level package.** A prime $\ell$ with $3 \le \ell$, $\ell \neq q$, $\ell \nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ which is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; an element $\varpi_t \in k_0$ lying in $A$ with $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   **Base-layer package.** An intermediate field $K_b$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ with $K_b = \bot$; a valuation subring $A_b \subseteq K_b$ with $x \in A_b \leftrightarrow x \in A$ for all $x \in K_b$; an element $\varpi_b \neq 0$ of $A_b$ generating the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Giving `fieldBar q M'` the $k_0$-algebra structure obtained by composing $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q} \to$ `fieldBar q M'`, there exist an intermediate field $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ and a valuation subring $W_0 \subseteq F_0$ such that the following nine assertions hold.
--
--   (1) $F_0$ together with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ spans everything: `adjoin k₀ (Set.range (algebraMap ℚ̄ (fieldBar q M'))) ⊔ F₀ = ⊤`.
--
--   (2) For $x \in k_0$: $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$.
--
--   (3) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring.
--
--   (4) The image of $\pi_0$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (5) There is $t \in W_0$ with the following property: for every polynomial $p \in k_0[X]$ all of whose coefficients lie in $A$, if $\mathrm{aeval}\,t\,p$ lies in $W_0$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0$, then every coefficient of $p$, mapped into $F_0$, lies in $W_0$ and in its maximal ideal.
--
--   (6) Let $g$ be a Laurent series in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose coefficientwise image in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, and assume: at every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of $j_q$ one also has $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of $g$; and the $R_0$-residue of $g$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$. Then the image of $g$ in `fieldBar q M'` under the inclusion `hle` lies in $F_0$, the resulting element of $F_0$ lies in $W_0$, and for every $c \in k_0$ with $c \in A$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of the $R_0$-residue of $g$, the difference of that element and the image of $c$ lies in $W_0$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (7) For every $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) and every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M') \subseteq \mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb Z)$, the automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ maps $F_0$ into $F_0$, and for $f \in F_0$ whose image again lies in $F_0$, $f \in W_0$ if and only if its image lies in $W_0$.
--
--   (8) For every intermediate field $K'$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ with $K'$ finite over $k_0$, every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and every $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to$ `fieldBar q M'` with each $a_i$ in the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$: if $c$ is linearly independent over $K'$ and $\sum_i (\text{image of } c_i)\,a_i = 0$, then $a_i = 0$ for all $i$.
--
--   (9) For every field $FSS$ equipped with a $\kappa$-algebra structure and every regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ from `fieldBar q M'` to $FSS$ — a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with a surjective residue map onto $FSS$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, inducing $A \to \kappa$ on constants and satisfying the same normalisation on non-zero elements — such that for all $f \in F_0$ one has $f \in R.\mathrm{integers}$ if and only if $f \in W_0$, both of the following hold.
--
--   (9a) For every $\mathrm{GaloisField}(q,2)$-algebra structure on $\kappa$, every proof that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) is a domain, and every $\zeta \in$ `Idx q`, there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity in $\mathrm{GaloisField}(q,2)$ and an isomorphism of $\kappa$-algebras $e$ from $FSS$ onto [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) (the fixed field inside the Drinfeld function field $\mathrm{Frac}(\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa)$ of the subgroup generated by the $C_s$-indexed operators $\mathrm{hFunctionFieldAction}\,q\,\kappa\,\langle(1,\zeta')\rangle$), such that $\mathrm{Nat.card}\,C_s =$ `placeWidthChar q M' s`, which for $q = 2$ is $12$ or $1$ according as $s.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen})$ is zero or not, divided by `placeRamificationJ M' s`; and such that for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, granted that `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and that $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1)$ lies in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) (the kernel of $(g,u) \mapsto \det(g)\,u^{q+1}$), one has for all $x \in FSS$ the equality, inside the Drinfeld function field, of $e$ applied to $R.\mathrm{resAut}$ of `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹` at $x$ with $\mathrm{hFunctionFieldAction}\,q\,\kappa$ at $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)$ applied to $e(x)$.
--
--   (9b) There exist a finite set $N$ of places of $FSS$ over $\kappa$, an assignment $Q \mapsto S_b(Q)$ of subrings of `fieldBar q M'`, ring maps $\varphi_b(Q) : A_b[X] \to S_b(Q)$ and $\chi_b(Q) : S_b(Q) \to \kappa$, and sets $D_b(Q)$ of places of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, such that $\#N = q+1$ and, for every place $Q \notin N$, all of the following hold: the image in `fieldBar q M'` of every $a \in A_b$ lies in $S_b(Q)$; $\varphi_b(Q)(C\,a)$ is that image, for every $a \in A_b$; $\chi_b(Q)(\varphi_b(Q)(C\,a))$ is the residue of $a$ in $\kappa$; $\chi_b(Q)(\varphi_b(Q)(X)) = 0$; $S_b(Q)$ is local with $\ker \chi_b(Q)$ equal to its maximal ideal; $S_b(Q)$ is contained in the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_b$, and every element of that compositum is of the form $g/h$ with $g, h \in S_b(Q)$, $h \neq 0$; $\varphi_b(Q)$ is formally smooth, formally unramified and essentially of finite type; every element of $S_b(Q)$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, and such an element lies in the maximal ideal of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ if and only if it is divisible by $\varphi_b(Q)(C\,\varpi_b)$ in $S_b(Q)$; for every $f \in S_b(Q)$ the $R$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $Q$ and its residue in $Q.\mathrm{ResidueField}$ is the image of $\chi_b(Q)(f)$ under $\kappa \to Q.\mathrm{ResidueField}$; the $R$-residue of $\varphi_b(Q)(X)$ has $Q.\mathrm{ord}$ equal to $1$; and $D_b(Q)$ consists exactly of those places $P$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ which are rational, for which every $f \in S_b(Q)$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$ with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f) \in A$, and for which, for every $f \in S_b(Q)$, the $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ is $< 1$ if and only if $\chi_b(Q)(f) = 0$.
--
--   Moreover, in (9b): the discs are disjoint, in the sense that if $Q, Q' \notin N$ and some $P$ lies in both $D_b(Q)$ and $D_b(Q')$ then $Q = Q'$; for $Q \notin N$ and $P \in D_b(Q)$ one has $0 \le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of $j_q$ in `fieldBar q M'`; and for every $\tau$ in the subgroup of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-automorphisms of `fieldBar q M'` generated by the automorphisms `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` with $\zeta \in$ `Idx q` and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, assuming $\tau$ preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$, every place $Q$ of $FSS$ satisfies: $R.\mathrm{resAut}(\tau) \cdot Q \in N$ if and only if $Q \in N$; and if $Q \notin N$ then $\mathrm{smulDisc}\,\tau\,(D_b(Q)) = D_b(R.\mathrm{resAut}(\tau) \cdot Q)$, where $\mathrm{smulDisc}\,\tau\,D = \{P \mid \tau^{-1} \cdot P \in D\}$.
--
--   This is the $q = 2$ instance, with the rigid-level guard $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$, $\ell_g \mid M'$, of the construction of a supersingular component of the semistable model of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$: it produces a discrete valuation ring $W_0$ on a $k_0$-rational model $F_0$ of the function field, residually transcendental over $A \cap k_0$, whose special fibre is identified with the function field of a quotient of the Drinfeld curve over $\kappa$, equivariantly for the level automorphisms, together with the residue discs attached to the non-exceptional places of that special fibre. It feeds [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointStalks_of_eq_two_of_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointStalks_of_eq_two_of_dvd).
